Nostradamus spent many years working in his tower, as a base to conduct his work as a visionary dictating his prophecies of the future in the form of [[Quatrains of Nostradamus|quatrains]]. He left many artifacts in his secret room including his [[Nostradamus' Scrying Glass|Scrying Glass]] with three [[Sentry Triclops]] [[Titans]] to guard it. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}} The accuracy of his prophecies led him to be branded a historical legend, however many accused him of being a fraud. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

Nostradamus would have visions of a [[Casterwill family]] traitor stealing the [[Ring]] of [[Kronos]], the [[Legendary Titan]] of Time and would travel to [[Prague]] to warn the Casterwill council there. {{source|The Power of Kronos}}

Many years later, his tower was swept by the [[Huntik Foundation]] and converted into a museum. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

After [[Stack]] informed [[Wilder]] that the [[Huntik Foundation]] were investigating Nostradamus' quatrains, Wilder and his team planned to discover the tower's secrets. Unbeknownst to them, [[Peter]], [[Billie]] and [[Annette]] were stationed there. After recognizing [[Hoffman]] from their files, Billie and Peter tried to stop [[the Organization]] team from accessing Nostradamus' secret room. However, they failed and were taken captive. They were later rescued by [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] team who, after defeating the Organization, recovered the Scrying Glass which translated the Quatrains and pointed them in the direction of [[Avalon]]. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

[[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] encountered Nostradamus in person when they were sent back in time by [[Kronos]] and [[Dr. Benway]]. He and [[Viktor Casterwill]] questioned why they were attempting to take the Ring of Kronos from the Astronomical Clock of Prague and pursued them. He summoned [[Sorcerel|Powerbonded Sorcerel]] but tried to prevent Viktor from harming Cherit and Sophie. However, he was overpowered by the corrupted Viktor but was saved by Lok and the [[Willblade]] who knocked Viktor out. After Sophie explained the situation regarding Kronos, Nostradamus invoked Kronos and sent them back home. It was only after returning home that they realised who Michel de Notre Dame really was and Lok was particularly frustrated as he had been so close to finding out the truth behind the quatrains. {{Source|The Power of Kronos}}.

On the longest night of the year, the Huntik team traveled to [[Nostradamus' Tomb]] in [[Salon Graveyard]] where they found the final prophecies ordering them to fly the [[Phoenix]] into the centre of the [[Spiral Mark]] and for the [[Champion of Casterwill]] to drive the Willblade into the mark to destroy it. {{source|Words from Eathon}} The prophecy later turned out to have been faked by [[the Betrayer]] and instead caused the [[Red Comet]] to change course for Earth, bringing back the [[Nullifiers]] in the process. {{source|The Spiral Mark}}

During the final battle against the Betrayer, Sophie used the [[Cypherdex]] to find Nostradamus' real prophecy that "the Betrayer fears his own medicine", which helped the Huntik team to defeat the Betrayer by literally stabbing him in the back. {{source|Dante's Return}}
